}}

 * The ability has two main components:
** [[File:Dota2 Condition-1.png|1|21px]] {{Symbol|Affect|Self}}
*** {{Symbol|bonus ls}}
**** [[Lifesteal]] for the full value ([[before reductions]]) regardless of the damage instance value in the {{M|combat log}}, this includes from the following sources:
***** {{M|Damage block}} sources.
***** {{M|Damage negation}} sources.
***** {{M|Incoming damage}} manipulation sources on the affected target.
**** Does not lifesteal from the following units:
***** {{M|Buildings}}
***** {{M|Ward-type units}}.
*** {{Symbol|Modifier|Stack}} {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Health}}
**** Grants 1 stack of permanent max {{M|health}} bonus per last hit credited to N'aix on certain units, this is an {{M|on-death effect}}.
**** Considers {{A|Meepo|Divided We Stand|text=Meepo Clones}} and the {{H|Spirit Bear}} as heroes, and the following units as creeps:
***** {{M|Attached-type units}}.
***** {{M|Buildings}}
***** Other {{M|creep-heroes}}.
***** {{M|Illusions}}
***** {{M|The Double}}
***** {{M|Ward-type units}}.
** [[File:Dota2 Condition-2.png|2|21px]] {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
*** {{Symbol|Attack Damage|Conditional}}
**** Feast is a bonus [[conditional attack damage]] source and has the following properties:
***** The max health as bonus attack damage values are directly added to N'aix' attack damage in the {{M|combat log}} and not displayed on the [[HUD]].
**** Does not interact with the following sources:
***** {{M|Allied units|x}}.
***** {{M|Buildings}}
***** {{M|Ward-type units}}.
***** Percentage-based {{M|bonus attack damage|x}} sources.
**** Interacts with the following sources:
***** {{Symbol|Affect|Self}}
****** {{M|Lifesteal}} sources.
****** {{M|Critical strike}} sources.
****** {{M|Cleave}} sources.
***** {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
****** {{M|Damage block}} sources.
*** {{Symbol|Deny}}
**** Considers {{M|clones}} and the {{H|Spirit Bear}} as heroes; other {{M|creep-heroes}} and {{M|ward-type units}} as creeps.
**** Cannot deny the following units:
***** {{M|Couriers}}
***** {{M|Illusions}}

* The ability effects are applied as follows:
*# The {{M|lifesteal}}.
*# N'aix' attack damage instance.

{{Splreflectnotes
| name = Infest
| desc = Does not interact with [[Spell Reflection]] sources.
}}
{{Stealnotes
| name = Infest
| desc = The same {{Symbol|Target|Unit}} targeted unit can be affected by multiple Infest sources.<br><br>However, the health bonus granted do not stack.<br><br>If the targeted unit is a creep, only the first Infest source can control the unit and can use the {{A|Lifestealer|Consume}} {{M|sub-ability}}.
}}
{{Splduplicatenotes
| name = Infest
| desc = {{Symbol|bonus agh}} {{A|Lifestealer|Consume}} only affects the primary {{Symbol|Target|Unit}} unit-targeted enemy.
}}

 {{Infestcard}}

* The ability has four main components:
** [[File:Dota2 Condition-1.png|1|21px]]
*** Considers {{M|clones}}, {{M|illusions}}, and {{M|creep-heroes}} as heroes, and has the following mechanics restrictions:
**** {{Symbol|Affect|Ally}}
***** Can be cast on but cannot control allied heroes.
**** Cannot be cast on the following units:
***** {{M|Enemy heroes|x}}.
****** {{cf|aghnotes}}
******* Acquiring the {{M|Aghanim's Scepter|text=ability upgrade}} removes this restriction.
******* Cannot control enemy heroes regardless.
***** {{M|Couriers}}.
***** {{U|Undying Zombie|text=Undying Zombies}}.
***** {{M|Spell immune}} units.
***** {{M|Ward-type units}}.
** [[File:Dota2 Condition-2.png|2|21px]] {{Symbol|Affect|Self}}
*** Applies the following ability effects on N'aix upon cast:
**** Applies a {{M|basic dispel}} that dispels both {{M|buffs}} and {{M|debuffs}} on Lifestealer.
**** {{M|Disjoint}} incoming {{M|projectiles}}.
**** Both {{M|attack immune}} and {{M|spell immune}}.
**** {{M|Disarm}}
**** {{M|Hidden}}
**** {{M|Invulnerable}}
**** {{M|Root}}
**** {{M|Unselectable}}
*** Periodically moves N'aix along with the {{Symbol|Target|Unit}} targeted unit. This affects the following things:
**** Reappears at the target's current location upon exiting {{A|Lifestealer|Consume}} in any way.
**** All {{M|auras}} are now bestowed and centered around the affected target.
**** Ability effects that interact with heroes' presence react on the current target.
***** For {{A|Io|Relocate}}, N'aix exits the affected target after the effect delay.
*** {{Symbol|bonus cd}}
**** The ability [[cooldown]] starts upon exiting the affected unit in any way, not upon cast.
** [[File:Dota2 Condition-3.png|3|21px]] {{Symbol|Affect|Ally}}
*** Applies the following ability effects on the {{Symbol|Target|Unit}} unit-targeted ally:
**** {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{Code|life_stealer_infest_effect}}
***** {{Symbol|Health}}
****** Applies the max and current [[health]] bonuses utilizing the {{M|setting health}} mechanic.
****** This component does not affect {{M|ancient creeps}}.
***** {{Symbol|Movement Speed}} {{Symbol|a|Up}}
****** For heroes, grants the percentage-based {{M|movement speed}} bonus.
***** {{Symbol|fx|v}}
****** The targeted unit has an ally-only visual effect above it.
** [[File:Dota2 Condition-4.png|4|21px]] 
*** For all {{M|lane creeps}} and {{M|neutral creeps}}:
**** Converts the creep into N'aix' unit and instantly takes control over it.
***** The converted creep retains its [[health]] bar colors for camouflaging purposes.
***** Utilizes the {{M|setting mana}} mechanic, fully restoring the unit's {{M|mana}}.
***** [[Movement speed#Set Movement Speed|Set]] N'aix' base {{M|movement speed}} to {{Code|Self[[Movement Speed|MS]] × ({{calc|1+v1|v1={{#var:Infest type1 value2}}}} + {{ValueColor||{{calc|v1|v1={{Show|T|Lifestealer|v3r}}%}}|tal|x}})}}
***** {{A|Attack Damage|Reinforced}} units receive {{Show|A|Attack Damage|Reinforced|value5}} {{M|incoming damage}} ([[before reductions]]) from the affected creep.
**** For the {{U|Minor Imp}}, it continues its attempt to move to the last known coordinates of its set target, despite not being controllable.
**** {{Symbol|Health}}
***** Loses {{calc|v1*{{#var:Infest basic1}}|v1={{#var:Infest type3 value1}}|%}} max [[health]] per {{#var:Infest basic1}}-second interval, over {{calc|10000/v1 round2|v1={{#explode:{{#var:Infest type3 value1}}|/|0}}/{{#explode:{{#var:Infest type3 value1}}|/|1}}}}/{{Code|Undefined}} seconds.

